From 4c36e899dffee2869af9afd174346e3eb9a7d7ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FatTank <hao.lin@samsung.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:13:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] packaging: use llvm-strip for x86_64 archives

The platform builds with LLVM. Use llvm-strip for the LLVM package's
x86_64 static archive post-processing while keeping executable stripping
on the platform default. Copy the current __strip_install_post macro and
change only the brp-strip-static-archive argument. Do not override
__strip. Check that llvm-strip is available after native archive conversion.

This change must land after change 356627. Archive bitcode must first be
converted to native objects; llvm-strip is not a replacement for that
conversion. Keep find-debuginfo and the rest of RPM post-processing intact.

The previously validated llvm-strip packaging run changed only the 270
static archives. Differences in all 45 compiler-rt archives come solely
from the strip tool: ELF structure differs, but allocated section content
and symbol-to-member index mappings remain unchanged. Host and Tizen
GNU ld and lld consumers, including sanitizer, profile and builtins
runtime tests, passed; non-archive files were byte-identical.

This override copies tizen_macros:34-38 from rpm-build-4.14.1.1-1.4.
Synchronize it when the platform changes that macro. It covers every static
archive in this package buildroot, including compiler-rt subpackages.

For this revision, four small RPM fixtures exercised the macro with its
disabled comment line retained or removed and debug packages both enabled
and disabled; all four built successfully. For the no-comment version: Enabled: only archive stripping uses llvm-strip.
Disabled: brp-strip keeps /bin/strip, while archive stripping uses
llvm-strip. Complete build results pending for this macro override.

Limit the override to x86_64; ARM follows after archive conversion and
packaging validation on those targets.

Change-Id: Iac085555112855d60cc7591931e91466691db6b2
Signed-off-by: FatTank <hao.lin@samsung.com>
---
 packaging/llvm.spec | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packaging/llvm.spec b/packaging/llvm.spec
index 13cc3a09898c..3bffa7b82659 100644
--- a/packaging/llvm.spec
+++ b/packaging/llvm.spec
@@ -1,3 +1,12 @@
+%ifarch x86_64
+# From /usr/lib/rpm/tizen_macros:34-38, rpm-build-4.14.1.1-1.4.x86_64.
+# Replace only archive stripping; executable strip keeps the platform default.
+# brp-strip-comment-note is disabled in the platform macro (tizen_macros:37).
+%define __strip_install_post    \
+    %{!?__debug_package:%{_rpmconfigdir}/brp-strip %{__strip}} \
+    %{_rpmconfigdir}/brp-strip-static-archive %{_bindir}/llvm-strip \
+%{nil}
+%endif
 %define keepstatic 1
 
 # MLGO AOT support for LLVM MLGO (Ahead-of-Time compilation)
@@ -438,6 +447,7 @@ python3 %{SOURCE1005} --root "%{buildroot}" \
     --disassembler "%{_builddir}/%{buildsubdir}/build/bin/llvm-dis" \
     --nm "%{_builddir}/%{buildsubdir}/build/bin/llvm-nm" \
     --jobs 4 --address-space-bytes 4294967296 || exit 1
+%{_bindir}/llvm-strip --version || exit 1
 %endif
 
 %post -n clang -p /sbin/ldconfig
-- 
